{"id": "20461471", "revid": "473593", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20461471", "title": "Robin Tait", "text": "Robin Douglas Tait (14 April 1940 in Dunedin, Otago \u2013 20 March 1984 in Auckland) was a discus thrower representing New Zealand at two Summer Olympics: 1968 and 1972.\nHe represented New Zealand at six Commonwealth Games: 1962, 1966, 1970, 1974, 1978 and 1982.\nHe won the gold medal at the 1974 British Commonwealth Games in the men's discus throw event and the bronze in the same event in 1966. Tait carried the New Zealand flag at the opening ceremony of the 1982 Commonwealth Games in Brisbane, Queensland, Australia."}
