{"id": "20463106", "revid": "10202399", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20463106", "title": "Jardin des Ar\u00f4mes", "text": "The Jardin des Ar\u00f4mes is a botanical garden specializing in aromatic plants, located along the Promenade de la Digue, Nyons, Dr\u00f4me, Rh\u00f4ne-Alpes, France. It is open daily; admission is free.\nThe garden was created in 1983 on the banks of the river Eygues, and now contains about 200 types of aromatic and medicinal plants, including cedar, \"Cercis siliquastrum\", chestnut, cypress, juniper, olive trees, pine, and rosemary, thyme, and viburnum. It is now in a state of neglect."}
